      "amount": "1 teaspoon",
      "notes": "to taste"
    },
    {
      "name": "black pepper",
      "amount": "1/2 teaspoon",
      "notes": "to taste"
    },
    {
      "name": "terracotta dish",
      "amount": "1",
      "notes": "9x13 inch"
    }
  ],
  "instructions": [
    "Preheat oven to 375 degrees Fahrenheit.",
    "In a large skillet, heat the olive oil over medium heat and cook the sliced chorizo until browned.",
    "In a large bowl, whisk together the beaten eggs, ricotta cheese, chopped parsley, chopped oregano, salt, and black pepper.",
    "Add the cooked chorizo to the egg mixture and stir to combine.",
    "Pour the mixture into the terracotta dish and smooth the top.",
    "Drizzle the lacquer glaze over the top of the casserole.",
    "Bake the casserole for 35 minutes, or until the edges are golden brown and the center is set.",
    "Remove the casserole from the oven and let it cool for 10 minutes before serving.",
    "Serve the casserole hot, garnished with additional parsley and oregano if desired."
  ],
